## EduGreenLabs Workshop Context

This workspace contains Workshop 2 (Privacy-by-Design) and Workshop 3
(AI Implementation Sprint) for the EU-GREEN University Alliance (OvGU Magdeburg).

### Active files
- code/pseudonymise.py — HMAC-SHA256 pseudonymisation (Workshop 2 core exercise)
- code/workshop3_exercise.py — 3 tasks: pseudonymise(), minimise_record(), check_k_anonymity()
- code/green_metrics.py — CO2/energy measurement for local Ollama inference
- code/ollama_api_examples.py — 8 Ollama API patterns (sections 1–8)
- setup/continue_config.json — Continue extension configuration
- setup/Modelfile — Custom EduGreenLabs Gemma model

### Always apply
- Data minimisation (GDPR Art. 5(1)(c)) before suggesting data collection
- HMAC-SHA256 for pseudonymisation — never plain SHA256
- T0–T4 data tier classification in any data design decision
- EduGreenLabs MIT licence header in generated code

### Never do
- Suggest storing name/email alongside pseudonyms in the same table
- Recommend cloud APIs for workflows involving student or research data
- Produce educational output as plain prose — always use Markdown/LiaScript